{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 26, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and politician in the Crusader states of the Levant in the 12th century. He was the count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187.\n\n1152-1187 are the years of his reign.\n\nRaymond III was born in 1140 as the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. In 1152, he succeeded his father as count of Tripoli at the age of 12 after his father's death in a battle against the Muslim ruler Nur ad-Din.\n\nDespite his young age, Raymond III quickly established himself as a capable leader. He maintained alliances with the other Crusader states, including the Kingdom of Jerusalem and the County of Edessa, and worked to strengthen the defenses of his county.\n\nIn 1157, Raymond III led a campaign against the Muslim city of Shaizar, which was then ruled by the Zengid dynasty. The campaign was unsuccessful, and Raymond III was forced to retreat. However, the attempt on Shaizar highlighted the need for the Crusader states to work together in order to defend against the Muslim threat.\n\nIn 1164, Raymond III was captured by Nur ad-Din during the Battle of Harim. He was held prisoner for three years before being released in 1167. After his release, Raymond III continued to rule Tripoli and worked to maintain good relations with the other Crusader states.\n\nIn 1180, Raymond III married Eschiva, the heiress to the County of Sidon. The marriage brought the County of Sidon under the control of the Counts of Tripoli and further solidified Raymond III's power in the region.\n\nRaymond III's rule came to an end in 1187, when he was killed in the Battle of Hattin while fighting against the forces of Saladin. The battle was a devastating loss for the Crusader states, and marked the beginning of the end of the Crusader presence in the Levant.\n\n*Highlighted section part 1: Years of reign*\n1152-1187\n\n*Highlighted section part 2: Battle of Harim*\nIn 1164, Raymond III was captured by Nur ad-Din during the Battle of Harim. He was held prisoner for three years before being released in 1167.\n\n*Highlighted section part 3: Marriage to Eschiva*\nIn 1180, Raymond III married Eschiva, the heiress to the County of Sidon. The marriage brought the County of Sidon under the control of the Counts of Tripoli and further solidified Raymond III's power in the region.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -3.9219088648678735e-05}, {"token": "III", "logprob": -0.0001627074379939586}, {"token": "Count", "logprob": -0.3794739544391632}, {"token": "of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "Tri", "logprob": -1.4781842764932662e-05}, {"token": "pol", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "i", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "was", "logprob": -0.6085633635520935}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -0.12028805911540985}, {"token": "noble", "logprob": -0.09736596047878265}, {"token": "man", "logprob": -0.0022060361225157976}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.3376848697662354}, {"token": "politician", "logprob": -1.633162021636963}, {"token": "in", "logprob": -0.5585296154022217}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -6.318072337307967e-06}, {"token": "Cr", "logprob": -0.1536506563425064}, {"token": "us", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "states", "logprob": -0.021776961162686348}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -0.37853091955184937}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.005248221103101969}, {"token": "Lev", "logprob": -0.005118599161505699}, {"token": "ant", "logprob": -2.777537883957848e-05}, {"token": "in", "logprob": -0.3720087707042694}, {"token": "the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "", "logprob": -0.2295750081539154}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -6.9141146923357155e-06}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -1.1444026313256472e-05}, {"token": "th", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "century", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.011563774198293686}, {"token": "He", "logprob": -0.0030915